CORE
main.cpp
--cpp98 --show-goto-functions
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
must be one of \[derived::do_f
--
must be one of .*unrelated::do_g
^warning: ignoring
--
N5008 [class.virtual]/2, /7: the virtual call do_f() in numpunct::f
invokes the final overrider in the dynamic type, numpunct or a class
derived from it.  The front end lowers it to a call through the virtual
table entry `vptr->do_f', and remove_function_pointers took as candidates
every address-taken function of a compatible type, unrelated::do_g
included (bin53).  For an entry of a virtual-table struct type
(#virtual_table) the candidates are now the values of that entry in the
program's virtual tables; the assertion for a pointer matching none of
them keeps this sound.  With libstdc++'s locale facets, a facet's virtual
call had dozens of unrelated candidates (moneypunct's string accessors for
numpunct::do_grouping).  test_verify.desc checks the program's
behaviour.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program.
